  "wording_guardrails": [
    "Use floor-count, FAR, built-volume, and height proxy wording; do not call these measured building heights.",
    "Use OSM as proxy functional context; do not call it official zoning or imar.",
    "Use LST as response or validation, not as a predictor for LCZ-like morphology labels.",
    "Report remote-sensing semantic predictors with ablation because they can overlap with weak LCZ label information.",
    "Describe current network node/intersection fields as endpoint-derived proxies until a full topological network validation is added.",
    "Do not use the legacy 250/400/800 m Euclidean centroid-buffer road-context fields in the primary full baseline; retain them only for supplementary comparison.",
    "Describe green-space 2SFCA as an OSM and municipal-road-network accessibility proxy, not an official public-green-space or pedestrian-routing measure.",
    "Use the 800 m green-space 2SFCA log1p field in the primary context baseline and keep raw m2/person values for descriptive reporting.",
    "Describe street-frontage fields as road-buffer proxies, not cadastral frontage or measured setbacks.",
    "Treat current block-permeability fields as experimental and exclude them from first baselines after the 2026-06-18 visual QA failure.",
    "Report explicit motorway sensitivity for road-density reach metrics using YOLTIP=OTOYOL.",
    "Do not describe the explicit-motorway sensitivity as removing every ramp or grade-separated road because some visually similar features remain coded as CADDE or SOKAK."
  ]
